-- Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign - the Burbs monsters, the Burbs
-- D-bees as creatures, and the book's seven notable people with a stat block.
-- Nine creatures (migration 074) and seven notable NPCs (migration 072), with
-- their attacks in stat_attacks (migration 073).
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/add-cwc-creatures.sql
--
-- WHAT IS HERE:
--   * the three Monsters Common to the Burbs (printed 211-214): the Devil
--     Sloth (211-212), the Vampire Flat Worm (212) and the Spiny Ravager
--     (212-214, its stat block on 214). playable 0;
--   * the six Burbs D-bees as their NPC view (printed 202-211). They are also
--     published classes, and their slugs match the class ids, as Madhaven's and
--     New West's playable rows do. playable is 1 on these six only. Each row
--     agrees with its class on every shared figure (attributes, Horror Factor,
--     P.P.E., S.D.C., H.P., M.D.C. and I.S.P. shapes), checked by script
--     against the class markdown, which is identical to production's;
--   * Erin Tarn (printed 14-16), Sir Winslow Thorpe (16-18), Lt. Jack "Crazy"
--     Cavanaugh (190, the NTSET quick stats), Emperor Karl Prosek (214-215),
--     Joseph Prosek II (215-216), General Cabot (217-218) and General Ross
--     Underhill (218-219).
--
-- NAMES: the heading is stored as name and the person as real_name. Thorpe's
-- True Name line reads Winslow J. Thorpe; Tarn's reads Erin Tarn. Cabot has no
-- True Name line: his heading is "General Cabot" and the text calls him
-- "General Marshall Cabot", so real_name is Marshall Cabot (Marshall could be
-- read as a rank; noted on the row). The book never calls him Joseph.
--
-- TWO BOOKS STAT TARN AND THORPE. Rifts World Book 4: Africa (the EARLIER
-- book, p.147-150) printed both first; this book is later and wins. Where the
-- figures differ, Africa's are in the row's notes as the losing reading:
-- Tarn's M.A. 24 and Spd 15 (here 23 and 13, the book saying she has slowed),
-- and Africa's skill list (Writing in, Lore: Magic out); Thorpe's 9th level,
-- Spd 17, 70 H.P., 74 I.S.P., 1D8 karate kick, age about 30, fifteen lower
-- skill percentages, and a Wilk's 320 and laser rifle in place of the Triax
-- guns. Tarn's 14th level, H.P. 70, S.D.C. 25, 60 M.D.C. leaf armor and four
-- attacks, and Thorpe's S.D.C. 82, 110 + 50 M.D.C. armor, five attacks and
-- the rune flail Isabart Wind, are the same in both.
--
-- A notable's mdc is the being's own; body armor and cyber-armor are in
-- weapons_and_equipment or bonuses_note, as for every non-M.D.C. person.
--
-- BOOK SLIPS, STORED AS PRINTED: the Emperor is "in his late 50's" in the
-- introduction and 61 in the stat block (61 stored, the other noted); Joseph
-- II's weight is a bare 182 (pounds read from the 81.5 kg beside it);
-- Underhill's 5 ft 8 in is given as 1.65 m, and 140 lbs is stored for a
-- P.S. 22 soldier; the Trimadore's bonus lines repeat the Vanguard Brawler's
-- word for word (as the class does); the Kremin's one Multi-Weapon Blade and
-- Sheath is printed "60 each"; the Spiny Ravager's bite prints 1D4x10 with no
-- unit (stored as M.D., like every other attack it has); the Vampire Flat
-- Worm's M.E. prints ",N/A"; Cavanaugh's pistol range prints "400 ft/122".
--
-- RENDERED at 200 dpi (pymupdf doc[N] = printed N), every number read off the
-- render, not the text layer, which carries this book's digit cipher (the
-- Devil Sloth's 2D4xlOO is set that way in the PDF itself): printed 14, 15, 16,
-- 17, 18, 190, 211, 212, 214, 215, 216, 217, 218 and 219 in this pass, and
-- 202-211 from the class pass; Africa printed 147 and 149 for the losing
-- readings. Every creature row passes creatureFormulaGaps, the grammar the
-- endpoint rolls with. Prose fields are short paraphrases; an 8-word shingle
-- check against the cache text of the cited pages finds none.

INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES
('devil-sloth', 'Devil Sloth', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Considered anarchist or evil; an animal predator', '{"IQ":"1D4+2","MA":"1D6","ME":"1D6","PS":"6D6+6","PP":"3D6","PE":"4D6+6","PB":"1D6","Spd":"4D6"}', NULL, NULL, '2D4x100', '6D6+10', NULL, 'A Mega-Damage creature. I.Q. is a high animal intelligence. P.S. is supernatural. The M.D.C. line is set in the PDF itself with the digit cipher (2D4xlOO); 2D4x100 is the only reading.', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":5}', 'Saving throws: Horror Factor +6; most diseases, poisons and toxins +5.', 'Tracks rotting food or a blood scent at 80%, swims 70%, climbs 60%, and digs well.', 'The lumps on its head are combined eyes and sensor clusters: it sees the invisible and every spectrum of light and senses the supernatural as a Dog Boy does. It hates supernatural beings and will flee them or fight to the death. Keen hearing and smell; heals at double the rate of most animals.', 'None', 'None', '10-16 ft (3-4.87 m) tall', 'One to two tons', NULL, 'Forests of the south and east, the Ohio Valley, the Magic Zone, and Michigan, Illinois and Arkansas woodland; scavenges Burbs garbage. Rumored to have come out of the St. Louis Rift.', 'Travels alone, in mated pairs or in groups of 3-5; trainable like a dog, and Simvan Monster Riders love them; also used in arena blood sports', 'Supernatural beings; anyone who startles, corners or hurts it; it eats what it kills and attacks people only when starving or when they are dying', NULL, 'A horned, spiny heap of muscle with sloth-like claws that looks demonic but is a Mega-Damage scavenger. Jumpy and touchy, it rears up and shrieks a warning when startled, then tears into whoever threatened it, and has even taken on power armor and robots.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.211-212'),
('vampire-flat-worm', 'Vampire Flat Worm', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Considered anarchist or evil; an animal predator', '{"IQ":"1","MA":"N/A","ME":"N/A","PS":"1D6+4","PP":"1D6+6","PE":"3D6+6","PB":"N/A","Spd":"1D6+6"}', '4D6', '6D6', NULL, '2D6', NULL, 'An S.D.C. being, able to harm only S.D.C. targets; M.D.C. not applicable. I.Q. is printed as equal to one (low animal I.Q.). The M.E. entry prints as ",N/A".', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":2,"initiative":1,"strike":2,"dodge":3}', 'Saves vs disease, poison and toxins at +5; Horror Factor effectively has no effect on it.', 'Climbs like an insect 88%, prowls 76%, swims 50%.', 'Thermo-sensors and infrared vision. Its flat body on a hundred tiny legs slips through narrow gaps. Once its fangs are in it may coil around the victim to pin him, but it cannot constrict; a feeding takes 1D4 pints of blood, and it comes back to the same victim every night.', 'None', 'None', '4-10 ft (1.2-3 m) long', '10-30 lbs (4.5-13.5 kg)', NULL, 'The filthiest, most crowded parts of the Burbs; by day it hides in sewers, under rubbish heaps and debris and in dark, damp places', NULL, 'Preys on the sleeping, the drunk and the helpless, above all the homeless; also feeds on fresh corpses and animals', NULL, 'An alien night parasite, neither a true worm nor supernatural, that infests Burbs slums. It creeps up on a still or sleeping victim, rears like a snake and sinks two pairs of fangs in to drink blood, and an infestation is hard to root out.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.212'),
('spiny-ravager', 'Spiny Ravager', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Counted an evil animal predator, and taken for a demon by many in the wilds', '{"IQ":"1D6+2","MA":"N/A","ME":"3D6","PS":"1D4x10+15","PP":"2D6+10","PE":"5D6","PB":"1D4","Spd":"58"}', NULL, NULL, '2D4x100', '1D6x10', NULL, 'M.D.C. is the Main Body, 2D4x100 (destroying it kills the creature). By location: Spiny Lower Body 1D4x100; Tail 200; each Large Back Leg 200, each Large Front Leg 155; Tongue 50*; each of the 4 Sensory Clusters 90*; each of the 4 lower Small Front Arms 40*; each Eye 30*. * Small or hard to hit: a Called Shot at -4. I.Q. is a high animal intelligence. Spd 58 is about 40 mph (64 km).', NULL, 18, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":3,"strike":3,"parry":2,"dodge":3}', 'Saves vs illusion and mind control at +3; Horror Factor effectively has no effect on it. Blinding the eyes only halves its combat bonuses; the eyes and all four sensory clusters must go to blind it fully. Once enraged it may fight recklessly until it dies.', 'Swims 90%, climbs like an insect 68%, prowls 46%; recognizes a scent 75%, tracks by scent 65% and by blood scent 90%, following blood as far as a mile (1.6 km).', 'Holds its breath 3D4 minutes; thermo-sensors; sees the invisible and every spectrum of light; hearing so sharp it strikes targets it cannot see and is nearly impossible to sneak up on; leaps 20 ft (6 m) high and 60 ft (18.3 m) long; seemingly immune to poison, toxins and disease; shrugs off heat and cold, and ordinary S.D.C. fire does it no harm. A throat sack (a second stomach) carries four small clawed arms that butcher prey and can slash and parry in a fight.', 'None', 'None', '15-25 ft (4.6-7.6 m) tall; 25-60 ft (7.6-18.3 m) long', '12-30 tons', NULL, 'Plains and light forests of the US, Canada, Mexico and the Midwest, never dense forest or jungle; appeared only two years ago, probably from a Rift in the Magic Zone or Michigan, and now numbers perhaps 15-20 thousand', 'Hunts alone, in pairs or in groups of 3-5; Simvan Monster Riders adore them as mounts, pets and watchdogs', 'Humans and D-bees are its favorite prey, and it relishes Xiticix too; the CS has begun a campaign to exterminate it', NULL, 'A warm-blooded predator the size of a CS tank, plated and spined like an insect, that stalks caravans and raids the outer Burbs to devour people, pinning cars and trucks and ripping them open. Once it has tasted humans it keeps coming back.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.212-214'),
('nmbyr-gorilla-man', 'N''mbyr Gorilla Man', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any', '{"IQ":"2D6+4","ME":"2D6+2","MA":"2D6","PS":"4D6+10","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6+6","PB":"2D6","Spd":"2D6"}', 'PE+1D6', '3D4x10', NULL, '6D6', 'MEx3', 'Hit Points: P.E. plus 1D6 per level of experience. I.S.P.: plus 10 per level. M.D.C. only from body armor or magic.', NULL, 10, NULL, 'No unconditional racial combat bonuses; attacks and combat come from hand to hand training (typically Expert, Martial Arts or Assassin). Violent outburst when angry, embarrassed, frightened or frustrated: +10 P.S. (counts as Supernatural P.S. 19), +6 to save vs Horror Factor, +2 vs mind control, possession and psionic attack, +1 attack per melee; -2 to dodge, -30% on skills, cannot pull punches, fears nothing, and forgets mission, friends and its own safety.', 'Speaks native N''mbyr, American +20% and one language of choice +15%, on top of O.C.C. skills; the O.C.C. Related and Secondary skill picks are halved. Few are literate.', 'Sharp eyes with 120 ft (36.5 m) nightvision, great upper-body strength, and psionic powers.', 'None.', '1D4+2 physical psionic powers. 20% are Eruptors (major or master psychics): 1D4+1 physical powers plus one of Electrokinesis, Hydrokinesis, Pyrokinesis, Telekinesis (Super) or Telekinetic Force Field, at double range and duration and +1D6 damage. I.S.P. M.E. x3 plus 10 per level.', '6-7 ft (1.8-2.1 m) tall', '160-250 lbs (72-112.5 kg)', NULL, 'The Midwest, above all Illinois, Arkansas, Missouri and the Magic Zone, and the Chi-Town Burbs; they came through an anomaly at the Old Chicago ruins', NULL, NULL, 'Any Men of Arms O.C.C., Vagabond or Wilderness Scout, with O.C.C. Related and Secondary skills halved; Juicer and Crazy conversions do not work on them.', 'Ape-faced, long-armed, short-legged D-bees who love hard labor, wrestling and football and make fine climbers and warriors. Most are good-natured, but any of them can fly into a rage and maul even a friend.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.202-203'),
('tirrvol-sword-fist', 'Tirrvol Sword Fist', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any; most (60%) are good, and aberrant is the commonest evil alignment', '{"IQ":"3D6+1","ME":"3D6+1","MA":"3D6+1","PS":"5D6+6","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"3D6+6","PB":"1D6","Spd":"3D6"}', NULL, NULL, 'PEx3', '4D6', 'MEx2', 'A Mega-Damage creature with no Hit Points or S.D.C. M.D.C.: plus 2D6 per level of experience; most also get cyber-armor. I.S.P.: plus 1D6 per level. P.S. is supernatural and does M.D.', NULL, 12, '{"initiative":2,"parry":1,"roll":1,"pull":1}', 'On top of hand to hand (typically Expert, Martial Arts or Assassin): one extra attack per melee and paired weapons. Horror Factor save gains +1 at 1st, 2nd, 4th, 6th, 8th, 10th, 12th and 15th level; pull punch gains +1 at 1st, 2nd, 3rd, 5th, 7th, 9th, 12th and 15th. Natural W.P. Sword with the sword fists: strike, parry and disarm each gain +1 at 1st, 3rd, 4th, 6th, 8th, 10th, 12th and 14th level; a natural 17-20 is a double-damage critical, as is a strike from behind; a pulled blow can do whatever damage it chooses, as little as 2D6 S.D.C.', 'Speaks its whistle-and-click native tongue, American +20% and one language of choice +20%, on top of O.C.C. skills; 01-70% can also read American or another written language. Skills needing manual dexterity or precision are -10%.', 'Mega-Damage body; keen vision and good hearing; heals twice as fast as a human and regrows sword hands and other limbs within 3D4 weeks. Blades of M.D. bone replace the fingers, with a bony hook for a thumb, yet it can still work a computer. Double-jointed legs and prehensile feet serve as hands, even to drive.', 'None.', 'See the Invisible, Sense Evil, Sixth Sense, and one more Sensitive power picked by the player. I.S.P. is twice M.E., plus 1D6 per level.', '8-12 ft (2.4-3.6 m) tall', '250-500 lbs', NULL, 'A few hundred in the Burbs of the State of Chi-Town and fewer than a thousand in all the Americas; their origin is unknown', 'Many are champions of good, and some are rumored to have joined the Cyber-Knights', 'Tyranny and the forces of evil', 'Takes an adventurer, scholar or Men of Arms O.C.C.; Juicer and Crazy conversions do not work on them.', 'Huge, barrel-chested, grey-hided D-bees with a snaking neck and ivory bone swords for hands. Most are honorable warriors and superb swordsmen who speak in short sentences and are well paid as enforcers, soldiers, bodyguards and heroes.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.203-205'),
('quick-flex-alien', 'Quick-Flex Alien', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any', '{"IQ":"3D6","MA":"3D6","ME":"3D6","PS":"3D6","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"3D6","PB":"2D6","Spd":"6D6+25"}', 'PE+1D6', '3D6', NULL, '2D6', NULL, 'Hit Points are P.E. at first level, +1D6 each level. S.D.C. is 3D6 before physical skill and O.C.C. S.D.C. are added. M.D.C. only from armor or magic.', NULL, NULL, '{"initiative":2,"roll":2,"pull":2}', 'On top of hand to hand (typically Basic or Expert): +1 attack per melee, +1 to strike with modern guns or bow and arrow, paired weapons, and an automatic dodge like the Commando hand to hand. Horror Factor not applicable. Jumpy, hyper and easily bored; with a human O.C.C. every skill but Physical and Rogue skills is -10%.', 'Quick-Flex Rogue R.C.C., bonuses first: +20% Escape Artist, +20% Pick Locks, +15% Pick Pockets, +14% Streetwise, +10% each to Find Contraband, Land Navigation and Prowl; +20% to American and one other language; a Physical skill; Hand to Hand: Basic; W.P. Energy Pistol; W.P. Automatic Pistol or Sub-Machinegun. Related: 6, and 1 more at 3, 6, 10, 14. Secondary: 6, and 1 more at 3, 7, 10. Nine in ten cannot read.', 'Reflexes and speed about equal to a Juicer or Crazy; ambidextrous; leaps 8 feet (2.4 m) high or across from a standstill, 4 feet (1.2 m) more with a run.', 'None.', 'None.', '5 ft to 5 ft 6 in (1.5-1.65 m) tall', '100-150 lbs (45-67.5 kg)', NULL, 'Across North America, mostly the Midwest; about a million in all', NULL, NULL, 'Optional: an adventurer, scholar or Men of Arms O.C.C. may replace the Quick-Flex Rogue R.C.C.; Juicer and Crazy conversions work but cut life expectancy after augmentation by 25%. Tends to avoid those, full bionics and study-heavy careers.', 'The textbook D-bee: at a glance human, until you notice the big eyes, long face and pinhole nostrils. A racing metabolism makes it small, hyper and as quick as a Juicer, so it makes a natural gunman, thief, pilot or acrobat.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.205-206'),
('vanguard-brawler', 'Vanguard Brawler', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any; a third are anarchist and two thirds evil (33% / 66%)', '{"IQ":"3D6+2","MA":"2D6","ME":"3D6","PS":"4D6+4","PP":"3D6+4","PE":"4D6+4","PB":"2D6","Spd":"3D6"}', NULL, NULL, 'PEx2', '1D6', NULL, 'A Mega-Damage creature with no Hit Points or S.D.C. M.D.C. rises 1D6 each level; armor or magic can add more.', NULL, 11, '{"initiative":2,"roll":2,"pull":2}', 'On top of hand to hand (typically Expert, Martial Arts or Assassin): one extra attack per melee. Saves: possession +1, disease and poison +1, and Horror Factor +1 at each of levels 1-6, 8, 10, 12, 14. The high P.E. makes most resistant to magic, disease and poison. Clearly inhuman; the back spines mean human armor and clothing must be customized.', 'Vanguard Brawler Thug R.C.C., bonuses first: +20% Basic Math, +16% each to Intelligence and Streetwise, +15% each to Find Contraband and Land Navigation, +10% each to Pilot Hover Vehicle, Prowl and Track (humanoids); +20% to American and one other language; Body Building; Boxing or Wrestling; Gymnastics or Acrobatics; Hand to Hand: Expert; W.P. Energy Rifle and one more W.P. Related: 5, and 2 more at 2, 5, 8, 12. Secondary: 5, and 1 more at 3, 6, 9, 12. Scent tracking 30% (+10% on blood), climbing 68/56%, each +2% a level. Seven in ten cannot read.', 'Tough, scaly Mega-Damage hide good for only a few blasts; keen hearing and smell; sees infrared; a natural climber. Two rows of 3-6 hooked back spines gouge anything that jumps on its back, and their pattern tells one Brawler from another.', 'By O.C.C. only; most do not pursue it.', 'None.', '6-7 ft (1.8-2.1 m) tall', '220-320 lbs (99-144 kg)', NULL, 'Fewer than half a million across the continent, most in the Midwest; they cluster in family clans and gangs of their own kind', NULL, NULL, 'Optional: nearly any adventurer, scholar or Men of Arms O.C.C. may replace the Thug R.C.C.; Juicer and Crazy augmentation fails on their alien bodies.', 'Pale blue-green, scaly, spine-backed D-bees who lead street gangs and hire out as bounty hunters, slavers, hit men, enforcers and mercenaries. Brutal with fists and threats, they are also shrewd strategists who lead like crime bosses.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.206-208'),
('trimadore', 'Trimadore', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but most are anarchist and unprincipled', '{"IQ":"3D6","MA":"3D6","ME":"3D6","PS":"3D6","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6","PB":"2D4","Spd":"3D6"}', 'PE+1D6', '2D6', NULL, '1D6', '2D4x10+ME', 'Hit Points are P.E. at first level, +1D6 each level. S.D.C. is 2D6 before physical skills. I.S.P. rises 2D4 a level. M.D.C. by armor only; the home-built armor they start with has 50-100 M.D.C.', NULL, 9, '{"initiative":2,"roll":2,"pull":2}', 'On top of hand to hand (typically Basic or Expert): one extra attack per melee. Saves: possession +1, disease and poison +1, and Horror Factor +1 at each of levels 1-6, 8, 10, 12, 14. These lines repeat the Vanguard Brawler bonuses word for word and are stored as printed, a possible copy slip for a gentle race. Clearly inhuman; disguise is impossible.', 'Trimadore Mechanic R.C.C., bonuses first: +30% Basic and Advanced Math; +20% each to Armorer, Computer Operation and Recognize Weapon Quality; +15% Mechanical Engineer; +10% each to Computer Programming, Electrical Engineer, Military Fortifications, Pilot Hover Vehicle and one Pilot skill; +20% to American and one other language; +15% literacy in one Earth language; one W.P.; Hand to Hand: Basic. Related: 6, and 2 more at 3, 6, 9, 12. Secondary: 5, and 1 more at 4, 8, 12. Every one reads a language besides its own.', 'Flawless eyesight, sharp hearing, a fine sense of touch and a near-savant gift for machines; the long arms reach farther than human arms.', 'Techno-Wizardry fascinates them; other magic is not pursued.', 'Four powers: Telemechanics, Speed Reading, Object Read, Mind Block. I.S.P. is 2D4x10 + M.E., rising 2D4 a level.', '7-8 ft (2.1-2.4 m) tall; thin and gangly', '180-220 lbs (81-99 kg)', NULL, 'Rare: under a quarter million anywhere, and perhaps fewer than 100,000 on Earth', NULL, NULL, 'Optional: Scholar, Cyber-Doc, Operator or Techno-Wizard in place of the Trimadore Mechanic R.C.C.', 'Tall, gangly D-bees with a long thick neck, a small head and two-fingered hands, also called Fixers. Quiet, peaceful tinkerers who are forever taking machines apart and cobbling them back together, they make natural Operators and Techno-Wizards and mostly shun combat.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.208-209'),
('kremin-cyborg', 'Kremin Cyborg', 'alien', 'rifts', 1, 'Unknown; most seem anarchist or unprincipled, but blockers in their brains stop anyone reading their thoughts', '{"IQ":"3D6","MA":"3D6","ME":"3D6+4","PS":"1D6+22","PP":"1D4+22","PE":"N/A","PB":"1D6+6","Spd":"132"}', NULL, NULL, '280', '1D4', NULL, 'A full-conversion alien cyborg with no Hit Points or S.D.C.; M.D.C. is the Main Body. By location: Main Body 280, Head 110, each Leg 130, each Arm 95, each Foot 50, each Hand 30, Multi-Weapon Blade and Sheath 60 (printed as one item, "60 each"). P.S., P.P. and Spd are bionic; P.S. and P.P. are printed 22+1D6 and 22+1D4, P.B. 6+1D6; P.E. not applicable. Spd 132 is 90 mph (148 km).', NULL, 9, NULL, 'Hand to Hand: Expert. Brain blockers: +2 to save vs psionic attack, +3 vs illusions and hypnosis, +6 vs possession. Horror Factor save gains +1 at each even level from 2 to 14 (printed under an R.C.C. Skills heading). Clearly a cyborg; disguise is impossible.', 'Skills are essentially the CS Technical Officer''s (Rifts RPG); uses the ''Borg experience table. A built-in translator lets it speak every Earth language at 96%.', 'Psionic dampers in the living brain work as a permanent Mind Block against reading thoughts, emotions or aura. Nano restorers mend damage, folding salvaged Earth plating, circuits and whole limbs into the alien body. Bionics of note: finger jack and headjack, amplified hearing, translator, full optics, molecular analyzer, voice amplifier, radio, laser finger tool, climb cord and hidden compartments.', 'None.', 'None.', '8 feet tall (2.4 m)', '600 pounds (270 kg)', NULL, 'Driven out of CS lands to Michigan, Free Quebec, Minnesota, Texas and the wild west; about three dozen came through, the CS has destroyed nine, and perhaps 30 (100 at most) roam the Americas', NULL, 'The Coalition States, which order every Kremin destroyed on sight', 'None; plays as the Kremin Cyborg R.C.C.', 'Alien cyborg explorers cut off on Rifts Earth when their dimensional portal broke down minutes after they arrived. They say they are peaceful envoys, fight mostly in self-defence and keep apart from everyone, but nobody knows what they really want.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.209-211');

INSERT INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES
('erin-tarn', 'Erin Tarn', 'Erin Tarn', 'Historian and Rogue Scholar; the Coalition States'' Enemy Number One', 'rifts', 'Human', '14th level Rogue Scholar (history and anthropology)', 14, 'Scrupulous', 'Around 67 (by 106 P.A.); looks to be in her fifties', NULL, NULL, '{"IQ":19,"ME":24,"MA":23,"PS":12,"PP":10,"PE":22,"PB":14,"Spd":13}', 70, 25, NULL, 17, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":4,"strike":1,"parry":2,"dodge":2,"roll":2,"pull":2}', 'Hand to Hand: Basic at 9th level proficiency. Combat extras: a judo-style body throw, a critical on an unmodified 19-20, S.D.C. damage +2. Saves: magic sickness +12, magic +7, disease +6, poison and drugs +6, psionics and Horror Factor +5, coma/death +23%. Trust or intimidation 80%. Spd was 15 and she is slowing down. Rifts World Book 4: Africa (p.147) prints M.A. 24 and Spd 15; this later book''s M.A. 23 and Spd 13 are stored.', '[{"name":"Cook","pct":98},{"name":"Preserve Food","pct":98},{"name":"Mathematics: Basic","pct":98},{"name":"Computer Operation","pct":98},{"name":"Radio: Basic","pct":98},{"name":"Anthropology","pct":98},{"name":"Archaeology","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Demons & Monsters","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Magic","pct":98},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":98},{"name":"First Aid","pct":98},{"name":"Swimming","pct":98},{"name":"S.C.U.B.A.","pct":98},{"name":"Climbing","pct":98},{"name":"Horsemanship","pct":98},{"name":"Pilot: Sailboats","pct":98},{"name":"Pilot: Automobile","pct":98},{"name":"Pilot: Hovercraft","pct":98},{"name":"Pilot: Hovercycle","pct":98},{"name":"Language & Literacy: American","pct":98},{"name":"Language & Literacy: Spanish","pct":98},{"name":"Language & Literacy: Euro","pct":98},{"name":"Language & Literacy: Dragonese","pct":98},{"name":"Language: Gobblely (spoken)","pct":85},{"name":"Streetwise","pct":72},{"name":"Forgery","pct":90},{"name":"Palming","pct":55},{"name":"Prowl","pct":60},{"name":"Read Sensory Equipment","pct":90},{"name":"T.V./Video","pct":42},{"name":"Intelligence","pct":89}]', 'Percentages include her +5% I.Q. bonus. Running is in the book''s all-at-98% list but has no percentage of its own. Energy Pistol and Knife W.P.s at 14th level. Rifts World Book 4: Africa (p.148) lists Writing among the 98% skills and leaves out Lore: Magic.', 'A born leader with high intelligence, a curious mind, a strong will and a pleasant personality.', 'Casts no spells, but understands the basics of magic, spells, ley lines and pyramids and can read and use scrolls in languages she reads.', 'None.', NULL, 'Clock calendar, gyro-compass, universal headjack and ear implant; two bio-system fingers on the left hand and a bio-system spleen.', 'Weapons: a Wilk''s 320 (20 shots, 1D6 M.D.), a Wilk''s scalpel and wand, a big survival knife (1D6), a tiny penknife (1 point), a silver cross, six flares and a squirt gun against vampires. Armor: a 60 M.D.C. poncho of Millennium Tree leaf (the one intact of two from King Arr''thuu), a 50 M.D.C. Urban Warrior environmental suit, or another light suit of 40-60 M.D.C. A five-bud life wand from a Millennium Tree: superior healing of 5D6 five times a day, and five 7th level spells a day in any mix of water to wine, purifying food and water, curing illness, curing minor disorders and negating poison; +2 to save vs poison, drugs, disease and coma (already counted). Plato''s magic amulet: +6 to save vs magic sicknesses and protection from the undead. A bionic horse from the King of England. Travel gear including a translator, camera, pocket computer, disc recorder, communicators, binoculars and a first-aid kit with RMK and IRMSS nano-bots.', 'Rarely more than 3D6x1000 credits plus 3D4x1000 in gems or precious metals; spends freely on the needy and on books. Her pre-Rifts collection (mostly books, recordings and art) is kept at her home in Lazlo and is worth at least 150 million credits.', 'Intelligent, curious, observant, quick-thinking, modest, gentle and selfless; soft-spoken and motherly, yet brave, strong-willed and a natural leader who speaks the truth when others dare not.', 'Sir Winslow Thorpe, her protector; Plato and the folk of both Lazlo and New Lazlo; Tolkeen''s rulers; Lord Coake and his Cyber-Knights; Victor Lazlo; Lo Fung; King Arr''thuu; the Nog Henge Druids. Mages, mutants and D-bees hold her especially dear.', 'The Coalition States, the Federation of Magic, the Blood Druids, Mrr''lyn and other despots, monsters and criminals; the New German Republic is uneasy about her.', 'The most famous figure in North America, a silver-haired scholar whose histories and travel journals are read aloud across the continent and whose attacks on CS policy made her its most wanted subversive. She has been captured eleven times and always got away or was let go.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.14-16'),
('sir-winslow-thorpe', 'Sir Winslow Thorpe', 'Winslow J. Thorpe', 'Erin Tarn''s Cyber-Knight protector', 'rifts', 'Human (American Indian descent)', '10th level Cyber-Knight (psychic)', 10, 'Scrupulous', 'About 32', '6 feet, 2 inches (1.85 m)', NULL, '{"IQ":14,"ME":19,"MA":21,"PS":22,"PP":21,"PE":20,"PB":12,"Spd":19}', 74, 82, NULL, 19, 78, NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":1,"strike":5,"parry":6,"dodge":6,"roll":3,"pull":3}', 'Martial Arts at 10th level proficiency. Combat extras: paired weapons, a 2D4 S.D.C. karate kick, jump and leap kicks that are both critical strikes, a critical on an unmodified 19-20, S.D.C. damage +7. Saves: magic +3, poison, drugs and disease +3, psionic attack and Horror Factor +2, coma/death +10%. Trust or intimidation 65%. Cyber-armor: A.R. 16 and 50 M.D.C., worn with environmental armor of 110 M.D.C. Rifts World Book 4: Africa (p.149) prints him a level lower (Ninth, Martial Arts at 9th) with Spd 17, 70 Hit Points, 74 I.S.P., a 1D8 karate kick and age about 30; this later book''s figures are stored.', '[{"name":"Literacy: American","pct":98},{"name":"Language: Dragonese","pct":98},{"name":"Language: Gobblely","pct":98},{"name":"Language: Spanish","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Demons & Monsters","pct":90},{"name":"Anthropology","pct":80},{"name":"Paramedic","pct":98},{"name":"Mathematics: Basic","pct":90},{"name":"Radio: Basic","pct":90},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":85},{"name":"Streetwise","pct":56},{"name":"Pick Locks","pct":80},{"name":"Intelligence","pct":70},{"name":"Swimming","pct":98},{"name":"S.C.U.B.A.","pct":98},{"name":"Climbing (90%/80%)","pct":90},{"name":"Prowl","pct":75},{"name":"Horsemanship","pct":91},{"name":"Pilot: Jet Pack","pct":78},{"name":"Pilot: Hovercraft","pct":95},{"name":"Pilot: Hovercycle","pct":95},{"name":"Pilot: Power Armor","pct":85}]', 'No percentage printed for Body Building or Gymnastics (+5% on its abilities). W.P.s: Targeting, Chain, Sword, Energy Pistol, Energy Rifle. Rifts World Book 4: Africa (p.149) prints lower readings, alphabetically: anthropology 75, basic math 85, demon and monster lore 85, Dragonese 96, horsemanship 87, hovercraft 90, hovercycle 90, intelligence 69, jet pack 74, land navigation 80, pick locks 75, power armor 80, prowl 70, radio 85, streetwise 52 (all %).', 'A born leader with high intelligence, a curious mind, a strong will and a pleasant personality; a sound strategist and tactician and an expert against supernatural monsters.', 'None beyond common lore and rumor.', 'A master psionic with 78 I.S.P.: See the Invisible, Sense Evil, Mind Block and a Psi-Sword doing 4D6 M.D.', NULL, 'A bionic lung (gas filter plus oxygen cell), gyro-compass and clock calendar; cyber-armor (A.R. 16, 50 M.D.C.).', 'Isabart Wind, a Greater Rune flail from Lord Coake, forged by ancient dwarves of Coake''s homeworld: I.Q. 11 with a telepathic link to him, indestructible, blue-grey with a light blue glow, Scrupulous (an evil or anarchist being who touches it takes 4D6), 6D6 M.D. (double against vampires, the undead and the Apocalypse demons), and four air spells a day, from breathe without air, wind rush, fingers of the wind and float in air. Also a large silver cross, silver-plated survival knife (1D6+1), a pair of throwing knives (1D6), wooden nunchaku (1D8), Triax TX-26 particle beam pistol and TX-43 light assault laser rifle, a squirt gun and four TW rain flares. Armor: a 110 M.D.C. suit of knight''s armor from Wormwood or other environmental armor, and he can use most power armor. A bionic horse from King Arr''thuu. Camp and field gear with a medical kit (RMK and IRMSS nano-bots, laser scalpels), grappling hook, communicators and infrared binoculars. Rifts World Book 4: Africa (p.149) gives him a Wilk''s 320 laser pistol and a laser rifle instead of the Triax guns.', 'Rarely more than 4D6x1000 credits on him.', 'Quiet, serious, practical yet idealistic; calm and confident, he counts guarding Erin Tarn the honor of his life, values her life above his own and treats D-bees with the respect he shows humans.', 'Most Cyber-Knights; Katrina Sun (Isis), Victor Lazlo, Lo Fung, Sir Dred, Sir Prrcyvel, King Arr''thuu, his mentor Lord Coake, Plato of Lazlo and Erin Tarn; many nonhuman friends.', 'The Coalition States; evil and anarchist challengers who want to test a Cyber-Knight.', 'A Cyber-Knight of American Indian descent who volunteered to escort Erin Tarn to the Vampire Kingdoms and was swept with her through Wormwood, England and Africa before a Rift brought them home. He has sworn to stay at her side until death or her retirement.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.16-18'),
('jack-cavanaugh', 'Lt. Jack "Crazy" Cavanaugh', 'Jack Cavanaugh', 'NTSET Specialist; lieutenant leading a squad of six Dog Boys', 'rifts', 'Human', '8th level NTSET Inspector', 8, 'Scrupulous', '32', '5 feet, 11 inches (1.79 m)', '155 pounds (69.75 kg)', '{"IQ":14,"ME":22,"MA":14,"PS":20,"PP":18,"PE":13,"PB":9,"Spd":80}', 44, 32, NULL, 7, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":2,"strike":4,"parry":7,"dodge":7,"roll":4,"pull":3}', 'Printed as quick stats. P.S. 20 and P.P. 18 are cybernetic and Spd 80 is bionic. Hand to Hand: Martial Arts; paired weapons; damage +5. Saves: Horror Factor +6, psionic attack +4, possession +2, magic +1.', '[{"name":"Climbing (98%/98%)","pct":98},{"name":"Find Contraband","pct":54},{"name":"Lore: D-Bees","pct":70},{"name":"Lore: Psychics & Psionics","pct":70},{"name":"Computer Operation","pct":85},{"name":"Literacy: American","pct":75}]', 'Lore: Psychics & Psionics is printed as lore: psychic. No percentage for Boxing, Running, Pilot: Hovercycle or W.P. Knife; his NTSET O.C.C. skills are all around 90%.', NULL, 'Lore and personal experience only.', 'None.', NULL, 'Both legs bionic and plainly mechanical; bio-system arms, skin grafts and many internal organs that look fully human; multi-optic left eye, amplified hearing and sound filtration.', 'Vibro-knife in his left boot, neural mace, Triax TX-26 particle beam pistol (carried with ISS Command permission), a 9 mm pistol loaded with silver rounds, and a C-27 plasma cannon for big jobs.', NULL, 'Cagey, clever, resourceful, honest and loyal; fanatical about shielding humans from nonhumans and monsters, yet he trusts Dog Boys over most people and would lay down his life for another without hesitating. Liked by his peers and loved by his men and Psi-Hounds.', 'A six-Dog-Boy squad whose favorites, partners of five years, are Boris and Aldo; up to 40 police officers in a crisis; the ISS and military in city-wide manhunts.', 'Nonhumans, monsters and other dangers to the humans of Chi-Town.', 'A crafty twelve-year street veteran and among the most decorated and infamous agents, cleared for Chi-Town levels 1-30 but working mostly on levels 1-8; the most devoted member the "Nut Set" ever had.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.190'),
('emperor-karl-prosek', 'Emperor Karl Prosek', 'Karl Prosek', 'Emperor of the Coalition States', 'rifts', 'Human', '11th level scholar/diplomat/leader', 11, 'Diabolic', '61', '6 feet (1.8 m)', '165 pounds (74 kg)', '{"IQ":19,"ME":21,"MA":24,"PS":13,"PP":10,"PE":9,"PB":11,"Spd":9}', 58, 20, NULL, 11, NULL, NULL, 14, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":1,"strike":1,"parry":2,"dodge":2,"roll":4,"pull":4}', 'Alignment printed as Diabolic Evil. Hand to Hand: Basic; judo body flip; a critical on a natural 19-20; damage +2. Saves: Horror Factor +5, psionic attack +3 (M.E.). Trust or intimidation 80% (M.A.). Horror Factor is printed as Horror/Awe Factor. Up a level since Rifts Sourcebook One. The introduction places him in his late fifties; the stat block gives age 61, which is stored.', '[{"name":"Literacy","pct":98},{"name":"Language: English","pct":98},{"name":"Language: Techno-can","pct":98},{"name":"Language: Spanish","pct":98},{"name":"Language: Dragonese","pct":98},{"name":"Mathematics: Basic","pct":98},{"name":"Mathematics: Advanced","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Demons & Monsters","pct":98},{"name":"Anthropology","pct":98},{"name":"Biology","pct":90},{"name":"Computer Operation","pct":98},{"name":"Radio: Basic","pct":98},{"name":"Writing","pct":90},{"name":"Pilot: Automobile","pct":98},{"name":"Pilot: Hover Craft","pct":98},{"name":"Pilot: Jet Pack","pct":84},{"name":"Swimming","pct":98},{"name":"Intelligence","pct":78},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":90},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":82},{"name":"Concealment","pct":65},{"name":"Streetwise","pct":64}]', 'Percentages include the +5% I.Q. bonus. Hunting has no percentage. W.P. Knife (vibro-blades included) and W.P. Automatic Pistol at 11th level; W.P. Sword, Energy Pistol and Energy Rifle at 6th.', NULL, 'None beyond history and scholarship, which he uses to turn the people against sorcerers.', 'None.', NULL, NULL, 'Always carries a .45 automatic pistol, an S.D.C. dagger and a vibro-knife; in the field adds a CP-30 laser pistol and his favorite C-12 heavy laser rifle, and can use any CS gun. Owns a large collection of working pre-Rifts S.D.C. weapons with ammunition. Dress body armor of a new, light molecular-bonded material: 120 M.D.C., 15 lbs (6.8 kg), with the usual Dead Boy features, worn whenever he leaves the city walls and even at public addresses.', NULL, 'Stern, demanding, merciless, calculating and manipulative, yet charismatic and seen as a strong father figure; a megalomaniac ruled by his hunger for power and glory who loves and trusts his son without reservation.', 'His son Joseph Prosek II; General Cabot; opportunists who share his ambitions; the people of Chi-Town.', 'The Federation of Magic, whose terrorists killed his wife and younger son; the nonhuman and magic-using foes of the States.', 'The slim, greying ruler of the Coalition States, a master strategist, administrator and manipulator who has built his empire to last for generations and, after five patient years, is ready to launch a new war of conquest.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.214-215'),
('joseph-prosek-ii', 'Joseph Prosek II', 'Joseph Prosek II', 'Colonel; Head of Propaganda and heir apparent', 'rifts', 'Human', '8th level Military Specialist', 8, 'Aberrant', '29', '6 feet, 3 inches (1.9 m)', '182 pounds (81.5 kg)', '{"IQ":17,"ME":23,"MA":19,"PS":18,"PP":18,"PE":20,"PB":15,"Spd":15}', 52, 30, NULL, 9, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":1,"strike":4,"parry":5,"dodge":5,"roll":3,"pull":3}', 'Alignment printed as Aberrant Evil. Hand to Hand: Assassin; S.D.C. damage +7. Saves: psionic attack +4 (M.E.), magic and poison +3 (P.E.). Trust or intimidation 55% (M.A.). Weight is printed as a bare 182 with no unit; pounds is read from the 81.5 kg beside it.', '[{"name":"Literacy","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Demons & Monsters","pct":95},{"name":"Language: English","pct":98},{"name":"Language: Techno-can","pct":98},{"name":"Language: Dragonese","pct":98},{"name":"Mathematics: Basic","pct":98},{"name":"Computer Operation","pct":83},{"name":"Computer Programming","pct":68},{"name":"Computer Hacking","pct":53},{"name":"Cryptography","pct":78},{"name":"Radio: Basic","pct":93},{"name":"Radio: Scrambler","pct":83},{"name":"Surveillance Systems","pct":83},{"name":"T.V./Video","pct":73},{"name":"Forgery","pct":68},{"name":"Pick Locks","pct":78},{"name":"Intelligence","pct":76},{"name":"Read Sensory Equipment","pct":83},{"name":"Weapon Systems","pct":88},{"name":"Pilot: Hover Craft","pct":98}]', 'Percentages include every skill bonus (I.Q. +3%); literacy, lore, languages and basic math come from special education. No percentage for Body Building or for Robot Combat: Elite, which covers the UAR-1 Enforcer and SAMAS. W.P.s: Knife, Sword, Energy Pistol, Energy Rifle.', NULL, 'Lore and historical data only.', 'None.', NULL, NULL, 'Any he desires.', NULL, 'Quiet, calm, confident and decisive; calculating, deceptive and merciless, planning far ahead like a chess player. He sees power as a vast game he intends to master, thrives on crisis, hates defeat, and is utterly devoted to his father.', 'His father Emperor Karl Prosek; General Cabot and the other trusted generals.', NULL, 'The Emperor''s eldest son and heir, head of CS propaganda, whose campaigns won Chi-Town''s unshakable loyalty. Patient and content to serve at his father''s side, he already wields nearly equal power and may one day outdo him as a manipulator.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.215-216'),
('general-cabot', 'General Cabot', 'Marshall Cabot', 'General; Military Counsel to the Emperor', 'rifts', 'Human', '15th level Technical Officer (tech and science)', 15, 'Aberrant', '83', '5 feet, 10 inches (1.75 m)', '200 pounds (90 kg)', '{"IQ":19,"ME":16,"MA":17,"PS":12,"PP":11,"PE":13,"PB":8,"Spd":6}', 56, 24, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":5,"strike":2,"parry":5,"dodge":5,"roll":2,"pull":2}', 'Alignment printed as Aberrant Evil. Hand to Hand: Expert; S.D.C. damage +3. Psionic attack save +1 (M.E.). Trust or intimidation 45% (M.A.). The heading says only General Cabot and there is no True Name line; the text calls him General Marshall Cabot, read here as his given name (it could also be taken as a rank). Weighing retirement at 83, though in remarkably good health.', '[{"name":"Literacy","pct":98},{"name":"Mathematics: Basic","pct":98},{"name":"Mathematics: Advanced","pct":98},{"name":"Computer Operation","pct":98},{"name":"Computer Programming","pct":98},{"name":"Computer Hacking","pct":90},{"name":"Chemistry","pct":98},{"name":"Chemistry: Analytical","pct":98},{"name":"Anthropology","pct":98},{"name":"Language: American","pct":98},{"name":"Language: Spanish","pct":98},{"name":"Language: Techno-can","pct":98},{"name":"Language: Euro","pct":98},{"name":"Language: Dragonese","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Demons & Monsters","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Faerie","pct":98},{"name":"Writing","pct":75},{"name":"Swimming","pct":98}]', 'Percentages include the +5% I.Q. bonus; computer hacking is marked special. No percentage for General Athletics or Running. W.P.s: all energy W.P.s, Heavy, Automatic Rifles, Blunt.', NULL, 'None beyond tactical knowledge and lore.', 'None.', NULL, 'Artificial heart and kidney, bio-system polarized eyes giving perfect sight, a gyro-compass, a clock calendar and a headjack.', 'Favors the neuro-mace, the C-14 Fire Breather and an NG-57 Ion Blaster pistol; wears the new Dead Boy armor.', NULL, 'Quiet in public but outspoken with the two Proseks; clever, seasoned, confident, resourceful and imaginative, a general''s general who counts calculated ruthlessness a virtue.', 'Emperor Karl Prosek and Joseph Prosek II, whom he loves like family; he treats General Underhill as his pawn.', NULL, 'An old friend of the Prosek family who knew Joseph Prosek I, helped build the Chi-Town military almost from the start and knows every part of it. One of the great military minds of the age, he is among the very few the Emperor and his son confide in completely.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.217-218'),
('general-ross-underhill', 'General Ross Underhill', 'Ross Underhill', 'General commanding the 4th CS Mechanized Infantry Division', 'rifts', 'Human', '10th level Military RPA Elite Soldier (SAMAS)', 10, 'Anarchist', '44', '5 feet, 8 inches (1.65 m)', '140 pounds', '{"IQ":14,"ME":15,"MA":20,"PS":22,"PP":18,"PE":21,"PB":10,"Spd":12}', 69, 40, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":5,"strike":4,"parry":7,"dodge":7,"roll":4,"pull":3}', 'Hand to Hand: Martial Arts; paired weapons; every kick attack; judo body throw; a critical on a natural 18-20; S.D.C. damage +7 (P.S. bonus). Saves: magic and poison +3 (P.E.). Trust or intimidation 60%. Height and weight are stored as printed: 5 ft 8 in is given as 1.65 m (it is nearer 1.73 m), and 140 lbs is light for P.S. 22. Illiterate.', '[{"name":"Climbing (85%/75%)","pct":85},{"name":"Swimming","pct":95},{"name":"Demolitions","pct":82},{"name":"Demolitions: Disposal","pct":82},{"name":"Pilot: Tanks & APCs","pct":84},{"name":"Pilot: Hovercraft","pct":98},{"name":"Radio: Basic","pct":98},{"name":"Radio: Scramblers","pct":85},{"name":"First Aid","pct":98},{"name":"Streetwise","pct":52},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":70},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":68}]', 'No percentage for Boxing, Body Building, Gymnastics, General Athletics or Robot Combat: Elite. W.P.s: all energy weapon W.P.s, Automatic Pistol, Automatic Rifles, Heavy, Knife, Chain, Blunt.', NULL, 'None.', 'None.', NULL, 'Bionic left arm (P.S. 20, P.P. 18) with an E-clip port, laser finger blaster, explosive finger joints (3 on the little finger) and a particle beam forearm blaster; a bionic lung; sound filtration, amplified hearing, a universal headjack, a clock calendar and a gyro-compass.', 'Favors rail guns, a CV-212 variable light frequency laser rifle, the C-50 Dragonfire and C-14 Fire Breather, a vibro-knife and a neural mace. Now always goes into battle in a Super SAMAS, which he rates the greatest infantry equipment ever made.', NULL, 'Loud, gruff, outspoken and honest; fiercely devoted to humankind and to his troops, and merciless in battle to nonhumans and the humans who back them. Flamboyant, self-righteous and ruled by ego; his men would follow him into hell.', 'His troops; Emperor Prosek and General Cabot, who flatter his ego and aim him like a weapon.', 'All nonhumans and the humans who support them; the Legion of Dragons and the Federation of Magic among 94 campaigns.', 'A decorated hero of 94 campaigns against inhuman foes whom Prosek propaganda hails as the greatest CS commander since Joseph Prosek I. A glory-seeking human supremacist who fights beside his men, he is kept out of the Tolkeen siege to defend Chi-Town and send out monster-hunting squads.', 'Rifts World Book 11: Coalition War Campaign p.218-219');

